# 8. Human approval API

The project also has:

POST

/api/agent/approve

It receives:

* transactionId
* reviewId
* approved
* reviewerId

If rejected:

* mark review REJECTED
* close unresolved recovery
* create audit event
* do NOT execute anything

If approved:

1. Verify transaction.
2. Verify review.
3. Find AI decision.
4. Re-run deterministic policy.
5. Confirm policy still says ALLOW.
6. Confirm stored policy decision has not changed.
7. Prevent duplicate recovery attempts.
8. Mark review APPROVED.
9. Record HUMAN_APPROVED audit event.
10. Mark transaction EXECUTING.
11. Record EXECUTION_STARTED.
12. Execute through the Razorpay/Test Mode adapter.
13. Store recovery attempt/result.
14. Verify the outcome.
15. Mark recovered ONLY if the outcome is VERIFIED_RECOVERED.
16. Store actual recovered amount.
17. Record execution audit event.

If policy is no longer ALLOW, execution must be blocked.

